I'll create a modern, animated digital business card with a clean aesthetic. Here's the complete code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Alex Rivers - Digital Business Card</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
            min-height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
            overflow: hidden;
            position: relative;
        }

        /* Animated Background */
        .bg-animation {
            position: absolute;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            z-index: 0;
        }

        .floating-shape {
            position: absolute;
            opacity: 0.1;
            animation: float 20s infinite ease-in-out;
        }

        .shape1 {
            width: 300px;
            height: 300px;
            background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,255,255,0.8) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0) 70%);
            border-radius: 50%;
            top: -150px;
            left: -150px;
            animation-delay: 0s;
        }

        .shape2 {
            width: 200px;
            height: 200px;
            background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,255,255,0.6) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0) 70%);
            border-radius: 50%;
            bottom: -100px;
            right: -100px;
            animation-delay: 5s;
        }

        .shape3 {
            width: 150px;
            height: 150px;
            background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,255,255,0.7) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0) 70%);
            border-radius: 50%;
            top: 50%;
            left: 80%;
            animation-delay: 10s;
        }

        @keyframes float {
            0%, 100% {
                transform: translate(0, 0) rotate(0deg);
            }
            33% {
                transform: translate(100px, -100px) rotate(120deg);
            }
            66% {
                transform: translate(-100px, 100px) rotate(240deg);
            }
        }

        /* Business Card Container */
        .card {
            position: relative;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            border-radius: 20px;
            padding: 60px 50px;
            box-shadow: 0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
            text-align: center;
            max-width: 400px;
            width: 90%;
            z-index: 10;
            animation: slideUp 0.8s ease-out;
        }

        @keyframes slideUp {
            from {
                opacity: 0;
                transform: translateY(30px);
            }
            to {
                opacity: 1;
                transform: translateY(0);
            }
        }

        /* SVG Icon Animation */
        .icon-container {
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            display: inline-block;
        }

Here's an example of an animated digital business card using HTML, CSS, and SVG for animations:

**HTML**
```html
<div class="business-card">
  <div class="background">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 100 100">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="100" height="100" fill="#f7f7f7" rx="10" />
      <rect x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" fill="#fff" rx="5" />
      <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="#f7f7f7" />
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="content">
    <h1>Alex Rivers</h1>
    <p>Digital Nomad</p>
    <a href="mailto:alex.rivers@example.com" class="button">Get in Touch</a>
  </div>
</div>
```
**CSS**
```css
.business-card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

.background {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  z-index: -1;
}

.background svg {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.background rect {
  fill: #f7f7f7;
  animation: pulse 5s infinite;
}

.background circle {
  fill: #f7f7f7;
  animation: spin 10s infinite;
}

@keyframes pulse {
  0% {
    transform: scale(0.9);
  }
  100% {
    transform: scale(1);
  }
}

@keyframes spin {
  0% {
    transform: rotate(0deg);
  }
  100% {
    transform: rotate(360deg);
  }
}

.content {
  z-index: 1;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
}

h1 {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

p {
  font-size: 18px;
  color: #666;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.button {
  background-color: #4CAF50;
  color: #fff;
  border: none;
  padding: 10px 20px;
  font-size: 18px;
  cursor: pointer;
  border-radius: 5px;
  transition: background-color 0.2s;
}

.button:hover {
  background-color: #3e8e41;
}
```
**Explanation**

The HTML structure consists of a container element `.business-card` that contains two main elements: `.background` and `.content`. The `.background` element contains an SVG that creates a subtle, looping background animation using CSS animations. The SVG consists of three elements: a rectangle with a rounded corner, a smaller rectangle with a rounded corner, and a circle. The rectangle and circle are animated using the `pulse` and `spin` animations, respectively.

The `.content` element contains the text elements (h1, p, and a) that display the fictional name, title, and contact button.

The CSS styles the business card with a clean and modern aesthetic, using a white background, bold font, and a green button. The `.button` element has a simple hover effect that changes the background color when hovered.

